+**Verdict dances from FBX (`VerdictDanceCli`)**
+- Turns humanoid animation FBX files (for example Mixamo's "Victory" and "Defeated" idles, downloaded as FBX) into
+  `<name>.unity3d` bundles for `StreamingAssets/CustomDances/`, one per FBX:
+
+  ```bash
+  ~/Unity/Hub/Editor/6000.2.6f2/Editor/Unity -batchmode -quit -projectPath "$PWD" -logFile verdict.log \
+    -executeMethod VerdictDanceCli.Build --fbx "/path/X Bot@Victory.fbx" --name Victory \
+    --fbx "/path/X Bot@Defeat.fbx" --name Defeat --out <dance-library>/Verdict [--silence 60]
+  ```
+- Each FBX is imported as Humanoid, and its clip becomes a looping, in-place clip (root motion baked into the pose)
+  saved as a standalone `.anim`, so no mesh goes into the bundle. A silent track of `--silence` seconds goes with it:
+  without audio the player would restart a short idle every few seconds; with it the idle loops smoothly until the
+  bridge's timer stops it. The FBX files are copied into a temporary folder under Assets and removed afterwards.
+- The title is the file name (`Victory`, `Defeat`), which is what `JUDGE_DANCE_WIN` / `JUDGE_DANCE_LOSE` name.
+
